      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors report the case of a 48-year-old man with a history of coronary bypass graft 15 years earlier. The follow-up by routine chest radiography showed a right paracardiac opacity, which MRI conformed to be an aneurysm of the saphenous vein graft."},
